far cry 6 is a whole lot of far cry with  a ton of gameplay mechanics from the  series combined with the usual hilarious  mayhem you'd expect there are so many  systems at play here like light base  building the rpg-ish mechanics of guns  gear with stats crafting it can get a  bit overwhelming at first but we've got  your back in this video we're going to  tell you the most important things to  focus on first because you can choose to  dig into or even ignore many of these  things later on if you love far cry like  we do with all of its insanity and  plenty of flaws hit that subscribe  button and give us the old thumbs up  let's get to it let's start with the  things that go bang in the night and  also the day and pretty much all other  times in far cry  parkour 6 treats weapons in an rpg ish  fashion they have a ton of variables  special abilities mod slots and it's  pretty critical you know what to do with  them at first because they're very hit  and miss pun intended you can pick up an  amazing looking sniper rifle and  discover it's really just good at  alerting enemies and mildly irritating  them then the next minute you can pick  up a bland looking gun and build an  unstoppable killing machine that punches  way above your level  and to just put that in context enemy  and zone levels do really matter in this  game at least at first so here's how you  get around that there are two main types  of weapons you'll run across in the game  regular and unique and there are pros  and cons to each your first instinct  will be to run off and collect all the  unique guns the ones that come in these  nifty gator cases some of these weapons  are extremely powerful but they are what  they are you're stuck with the mods that  come with them and some just do not  perform then there are the regular  weapons that you pick up through the  game and they can be customized and  modded at will many of these start off  weak but with a few tweaks can become  incredibly powerful  at the start of the game focus on  building a suppressed sniper rifle with  armor-piercing rounds a good sniper  rifle will carry you through huge  portions of this world some enemies will  be absolute bullet sponges to rifles and  lmgs but one well-placed armor-piercing  round will zip right through their  helmet and end the fight before it  begins there are a number of ammo types  in the early game armor-piercing rounds  feel like it just trumps them all after  that focus your energy on weapons that  knock down enemies or apply status  effects like burning that means enemies  won't fight back while being on the  ground or you know running around on  fire plus it's just so satisfying on the  first island the humidor shotgun is  fantastic and can be found right here  finally don't stress too much about the  level of a weapon it seems to matter a  lot less than the mods you put on it  alright so let's talk about supremos and  wrestle their weapons but i'm the  ultimate badass with ultimate weapons  you say not necessarily  the supremos and wrestle their weapons  that you have access to early on aren't  automatically better than weapons you  find on the ground with supremos the  super backpacks in the game we'd suggest  you stick with the exterminator door for  quite a while the main reason is that as  the game advances you'll start to run  into helicopters and boy are they hard  to take down without this backpack as of  right now we haven't been able to snipe  chopper pilots and the helicopters  themselves can soak up huge amounts of  damage like multiple rpg hits and  dynamite the exterminador backpack is  the one thing that can reliably take  care of them a lot of the other ones you  get later are nifty but it's hard to  beat a good screen clear  i should keep looking  seriously though helicopters are a  problem even later level resolver  weapons like the pyrotechno without its  he tiki mod has a hard time taking down  helicopters but in a pinch when all else  fails go find a mounted weapon  and speaking of wrestle their weapons  are unique home brew arms and they're a  lot of fun but also don't necessarily  open up gameplay or tactics you couldn't  get from a good weapon build la  clavadora which fires a huge spike for  example is very satisfying but it has a  slow reload and low ammo capacity that  makes it less effective than a good  sniper rifle or even this massively  powerful computer shotgun  now can you upgrade them to make them  more fun yeah this game is far cry as  hell  so when it comes to stealth slow is fast  for a big portion of far cry 6 stealth  is the way to go because i'll keep  saying this enemy levels matter i tried  to yellow the original preview event and  had a miserable time getting killed by  higher level enemies i'm not even  someone who usually likes stealth but  taking down enemy bases checkpoints or  even doing main missions using sneaky  tactics will make your life a lot easier  and more enjoyable the game presents you  with a bunch of enemy types and  different ammo to combat each type but  honestly just sneaking up and putting a  knife in someone's back is the most  effective way to go as usual focus on  alarms and enemies that can call in  reinforcements first  now while you're taking down bases you  will have amigos with you that's your  pets in this game and they become more  powerful with training your first amigo  guapo has some abilities you should know  about and with some training can become  even tankier stick with guapo for a  while and really invest in this reptile  as a matter of fact you will spend huge  portions of this game sticking with  individual pets guapo can revive himself  in combat and regenerate health and as  counter-intuitive as this is you need  guapo to die a lot to get stronger to  level him up find a good road crossing  cause some chaos send in guapo and just  sit back and let him die and revive  himself and die a whole bunch poor fella  needs to learn how to stand on his own  four feet so don't get involved after  maybe 10 or 15 minutes you'll have  leveled that first ability and he  regenerates health during combat now  after guapo have tried a few other  amigos but it's hard to beat a murder  crocodile  nice boy  so when you get to base building there's  a lot of things you can do at a base  maybe too many my personal  recommendation focus on building things  that increase mobility because this  world is massive and you're going to be  doing a lot of running many of the  sections in far cry require huge  traversals some of them can be tackled  with vehicles and horses but plenty  can't i initially purchased the hideout  network to open up the wingsuit which is  a must for escaping bad situations and  getting to objectives quickly the  wingsuit can operate very close to the  ground and let you go far then i  purchased the banditos barrack to open  up a shop that lets you buy things like  parkour kicks that increase your  movement speed and the parkour strap  that significantly increases your run  speed with your weapon put away at  higher levels you can buy shoes that  increase your crouch speed you see where  this is going other than that you can  engage with or mostly ignore the other  things at your base as you like you  might not even notice some of the other  things here from other far cry games  such as special operations and bandit  operations there's some additional  rewards and xp you can get out of these  but they're very optional alright so now  let's talk about side missions because  they're more worth it far cry 100 does  that ubisoft thing where you're on your  way to a mission and 10 other  opportunities pop up to distract you the  difference with far cry 6 is that a lot  of these missions give you gear with  stat bonuses that can truly help your  speed ability to not be on fire  tankiness and amount of money you can  make things like that the gear itself  doesn't have levels but it can open up  different play styles i'm honestly  impressed with the number of creative  options gear can give you and if you  want to see what you look like with all  this different stuff on just go to any  base to see yourself in third person i  fully credit gear and a good sniper  rifle with allowing me to plow through a  level 9 zone when i was level 5. for  context on the first island it was  pretty rough trying to tackle a level 5  zone at level 3. so yeah gear matters  speaking of leveling it goes very slow  in this game and you can find yourself  gated out of certain areas unless you  play it smart with your build that being  said doing a host of side missions  treasure hunts clearing checkpoints  taking bases or hunting animals can  really help you level up more quickly  but if you've played ubisoft games  before you know how this works  then let's talk about upgrades and  resources there's a lot of systems at  play here in far cry 6 and a lot of  different types of things you need to  level your weapons special abilities  bases mod slots wrestle their weapons  etc they don't all make conceptual sense  for example it turned out industrial  circuits that i couldn't find for the  life of me to level up the pyrotechnic  came from trading meat if you get stuck  like i did and you can't sort out how to  get a resource head on over to this  nifty inventory tab for a full breakdown  some other little tips you can do are  remember to touch vehicles after they  blow up for scraps or even go buy the  scrounger gear from the banditos barrack  that lets you auto pick up resources  while driving by in a car  these tips should help you through a  good portion of far cry 6. the world is  massive and we're still exploring it so  tell us about your builds easter eggs  you found or anything else important  that we miss  seriously there's a lot in this game  also make sure to head on over to  gamespot's youtube page for our full  review and other guides thanks for  watching definitely feeling it  danny did y